🌸 Korean Quest
A free, cute, and effective Korean vocabulary learning app built with Python and Streamlit.

Try it live → https://k-quest.streamlit.app

📖 About
Korean Quest helps you learn Korean vocabulary through spaced repetition. You see a Korean word, type the English translation, and get instant feedback. The app tracks your progress, streaks, and learning patterns so you can see how far you've come.

Built for Korean learners at any level — from beginners building basic vocab to intermediate learners drilling less common words.

✨ Features
Spaced Repetition System – Words you struggle with appear more often

Real-time Feedback – Instant check on your answers with response time tracking

Dashboard Analytics – Accuracy by category, hardest words, learning curve, and more

Streak Tracking – Daily practice streaks with milestone celebrations

Word Search – Look up any word you've practiced and see your history

Achievement Badges – Unlock milestones as you progress

User Authentication – Secure signup/login with Supabase

Fully Responsive – Works on desktop and mobile

🛠️ Tech Stack
Category	Technology
Frontend/Backend	Python, Streamlit
Authentication & Database	Supabase
Styling	Custom CSS
Data Visualization	Altair, Plotly
Deployment	Streamlit Cloud

🚀 Getting Started (Local Development)
1. Clone the repository
bash
git clone https://github.com/Rav3nsteel35/streamlit_korean_app.git
cd streamlit_korean_app

2. Install dependencies
bash
pip install -r requirements.txt

3. Set up environment variables
Create a .env file in the root directory with your Supabase credentials:

text
SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_url
SUPABASE_KEY=your_anon_key

4. Run the app
bash
streamlit run Home.py
The app will open at http://localhost:8501

📁 Project Structure
text
streamlit_korean_app/
├── Home.py                 # Landing page
├── auth_functions.py       # Authentication logic
├── utils.py                # Helper functions (CSS, images)
├── korean_words.json       # Word database
├── requirements.txt        # Python dependencies
├── assets/
│   ├── styles.css          # Custom styling
│   └── download.jpg        # Mascot image
└── pages/
    ├── 1_Login.py          # Login/signup page
    ├── 1_Practice.py       # Main learning interface
    ├── 1_Dashboard.py      # Analytics & stats
    └── 1_Profile.py        # User profile & achievements

🗂️ Word Bank
Currently includes 100+ Korean words with:

English translation

Difficulty level (beginner, intermediate, advanced)

Category (education, food, emotions, etc.)

Frequency rank

Want to add more words? Feel free to contribute to korean_words.json!

